committee for the purpose of forcing a vote of want of confidence in the government and of destroying the bill. Finally he referred to the present Minister of Finance, and said that he had at the conclusion of the debate moved the six months' hoist. All of this is now on Hansard in the remarks of my hon. friend to show that those who to-day are members of the present administration were at that time seeking to destroy the organization of the Canadian National system.
Perhaps I had better read exactly what my hon. friend said, in order that there can be no misunderstanding. I quote from pages 743 and 744 of Hansard of March 7. 1929. He said:
